    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for the Austin Waves is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 79.74. Facing Kremer, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to a dynamic platoon advantage, and assuming he occupies the leadoff spot, his plate appearance projections are unmatched. **Jacob Wilson** also provides significant upside (66.55) against the high-strikeout arm of Peralta, while **Kyle Tucker** (63.91) remains a cornerstone start despite facing the southpaw Cameron, as his raw talent and park factors keep his floor well above the marginal threshold. These three represent our primary offensive engine, with **Gunnar Henderson** specifically acting as the catalyst for our Roto categories today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Jackson Merrill**, who held a 50.37 score against Logan Henderson. Despite the sub-3.00 xERA of the opposing starter providing a tough matchup, **Jackson Merrill** managed to stay in the UTIL slot by leveraging a 13% platoon efficiency boost. Conversely, **Wade Meckler** (42.35) and **Luis Lara** (42.99) sit dangerously close to our \"Below floor\" threshold. **Wade Meckler** suffers from a brutal L/L matchup against Gore, which severely suppressed his score despite the value of the leadoff position. We are monitoring **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Robert Jr.** closely, as both carry a 31% rain risk; should a delay turn into a postponement, we are forced to reach into a bench currently depleted by the injuries to **Jordan Westburg** and the scheduled off-days for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Heliot Ramos**. While **Coby Mayo** (44.86) is technically active, his low projection relative to our roster depth makes him the most likely candidate to be swapped should we need to protect our game caps if the weather worsens.",
